---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Terms and Conditions', path: '/terms-and-conditions' }];
---

<Base
  title="Terms and Conditions | Red Creek Outdoors"
  description="Terms for using the Red Creek Outdoors LLC website. Hunt and trapping terms are set in writing at booking, before any money changes hands."
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <PageHero title="Terms and Conditions" crumbs={crumbs} lede="These cover the website. Every hunt and trapping job gets its own written terms at booking." />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> October 20, 2026</p>

      <h2>Prices on this site</h2>
      <p>
        Prices are starting prices. Your final price, dates, what's included, deposit and cancellation terms are set
        in writing when you book. If the website and your written booking disagree, the written booking governs.
      </p>

      <h2>Deposit</h2>
      <p>
        Whether we schedule you for a hog trapping site assessment or book you a hunt, a $100 deposit is due once we
        confirm we can provide the service. The deposit is nonrefundable. Nothing is owed until we confirm.
      </p>

      <h2>Hunting laws</h2>
      <p>
        Every hunter is responsible for holding the licenses, endorsements, stamps and certifications Texas and federal
        law require for the hunt they book. Our hunt pages link to the official sources so you can check before you
        come.
      </p>

      <h2>Information on this site</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep season dates and rules current and link to the agency that publishes them. Agencies change
        rules. The agency's own page is the authority, not ours.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>{SITE.legal}, {SITE.city}, Texas. {SITE.phone}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
